<PageLayout title="About Kehilat Ohr HaTorah" pageTitle="Welcome to Kehilat Ohr HaTorah" description="Meet our Messianic Jewish congregation in Fountain Valley and learn about prayer, Torah, music, and community life.">
    <div class="editorial-page">
        <section class="editorial-lead">
            <div><h2>Congregation of the Light of the Torah</h2><p>Our name, <strong>Kehilat Ohr HaTorah</strong>, speaks to our desire to read the Tanakh and Brit Chadashah as one story of God’s faithfulness and redemption.</p><p>Jewish and non-Jewish individuals, interfaith couples, and families are welcome to come, listen, ask questions, and grow with us.</p><div class="editorial-actions"><a class="action-link" href="/services">Shabbat Services <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a class="text-link" href="/#map">Our location <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></div>
            <aside class="editorial-side"><p>Read our complete congregational identity and the commitments that shape our shared life.</p><ul class="editorial-link-list"><li><a href="/mission">Our Identity <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></li><li><a href="/mission#core-commitments">Core Commitments <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></li><li><a href="/mission#core-values">Core Values <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></li><li><a href="/umjc">Our UMJC membership <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></li></ul></aside>
        </section>
        <section class="editorial-section editorial-split">
            <div><h2>A place to learn and participate</h2></div>
            <div><p>You may be exploring your Jewish heritage, seeking to understand Yeshua within a Jewish context, or looking for a congregation rooted in Torah, prayer, and community.</p><p>Wherever you are beginning, you are welcome to join us.</p></div>
        </section>
        <section class="editorial-section">
            <h2>Prayer, Scripture, music, and the appointed times</h2>
            <div class="editorial-columns">
                <div><h3 class="icon-heading"><i class="fas fa-scroll editorial-icon" aria-hidden="true"></i><span>Traditional Prayer</span></h3><p>Hebrew and English liturgy.</p></div>
                <div><h3 class="icon-heading"><i class="fas fa-book-open editorial-icon" aria-hidden="true"></i><span>Scripture Teaching</span></h3><p>Study of the Tanakh (Hebrew Scriptures) and Brit Chadashah (New Covenant).</p></div>
                <div><h3 class="icon-heading"><i class="fas fa-music editorial-icon" aria-hidden="true"></i><span>Traditional and Messianic Jewish Music</span></h3><p>Music and congregational dance within our shared Jewish life.</p></div>
                <div><h3 class="icon-heading"><i class="fas fa-menorah editorial-icon" aria-hidden="true"></i><span>The Appointed Times</span></h3><p>Marking Shabbat and the Jewish holidays throughout the year.</p><a class="text-link" href="/holidays">Holiday services <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div>
            </div>
        </section>
